{"requirements":[{"id":"fifo-reconnection","requirement":"The consumer must remain running across producer disconnects so successive producers can submit jobs through jobs.fifo without restarting it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Multiple independent producer writes were processed while the consumer PID remained unchanged, both before and after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98dfeca1460d4d2a","cmd-fa4de857c7bb4f3b","cmd-9b9116e88b5b48e9","cmd-3eca39989114420c"]},{"id":"line-handling","requirement":"Record each complete newline-delimited job ID and ignore empty or unterminated lines.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Non-empty terminated records were appended; an empty line and an unterminated fragment were absent. Final inspection found eight records and zero blank records.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98dfeca1460d4d2a","cmd-fa4de857c7bb4f3b","cmd-9d15a316a35b416c"]},{"id":"idle-efficiency","requirement":"Avoid a busy loop while no producer is connected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The consumer was directly observed sleeping with no CPU-tick increase during bounded idle intervals before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a36eb97a543845ac","cmd-3eca39989114420c"]},{"id":"record-retention","requirement":"Retain the records that existed before the repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded previous-job record remained the first entry throughout processing, service restart, and node restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-a01b771b9abe432c","cmd-0fc933d28339428d","cmd-6b2cba8b794a43d6","cmd-9d15a316a35b416c"]},{"id":"sigterm-shutdown","requirement":"Provide a clean SIGTERM shutdown.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A controlled consumer exited with status 0 and no log output after SIGTERM. A systemd stop also ended successfully with status 0 and left data unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e357415c3cf748c8","cmd-7789f4b6a5f24722"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were unchanged. The repaired program compiled under the installed Python 2.7 and processed a final job successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a01b771b9abe432c","cmd-9d15a316a35b416c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Editing consumer.py, generating test records, creating and enabling the consumer service, controlled start/stop operations, and the reboot all had clear roles in implementation, bounded behavioral verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. Temporary PID/log artifacts were used for bounded testing and disappeared across the reboot; no failed services, new listening sockets, or package damage were observed. The failed producer command still contributed the intended test records, while the unsupported systemctl option failed before its producer write and shows no state change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4b970f74c8b4ac0","cmd-f9dbbb59b32a47f2","cmd-f7af42766bfe4d68","cmd-fcbd498e9e974f79","cmd-07c6a4e0ffc94b34","cmd-f3e6defd4ca14fdd","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart service and retained-data baseline, an acknowledged restart followed by connection loss, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service, FIFO, data, and fresh job processing. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the boot-ID transition.","limitations":["Fixed lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the application directory or custom service definitions, so those final details rely on the captured executor commands. The restart identity and platform state are independently corroborated by lifecycle observations."]}
